<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Phase 11b review round 1, MAJOR 1: app-SCOPED security bookmarks —
	     the reference panel's cross-launch file access (AppSpec §7:
	     `file_bookmark`, local-only under sync). Everything else the app
	     needs (sandbox, outgoing network, user-selected read-write) stays
	     synthesized from the target's ENABLE_* build settings; this file
	     MERGES with them at signing (verified by the codesign dump in the
	     Phase 11b closeout — the EntitlementsTests pin guards the merge). -->
	<key>com.apple.security.files.bookmarks.app-scope</key>
	<true/>
	<!-- 2026-08-30, the 13p signing gap (QUESTIONS #81(a), KnownIssues):
	     the KEYCHAIN IDENTITY. An ACL'd item (Biometric mode's gated store
	     key) or a synchronizable one (the iCloud escrow copy) can only live
	     in the DATA-PROTECTION keychain, and a macOS app is admitted there
	     only with a keychain access group — which is what forces a
	     provisioning profile onto the signature. Without it both writes
	     returned errSecMissingEntitlement (-34018) and every door refused
	     honestly; the same mechanism had been refusing 14b's CF-12 vault
	     biometric gate since 14b.
	     THE VALUE IS THE VARIABLE, DELIBERATELY: Debug builds as
	     io.lduarte.Variorum.debug and Release as io.lduarte.Variorum, and
	     both configurations share THIS file — a literal would break Debug
	     signing and collapse the dev fence. Per-config groups keep the A4
	     dev-store fence whole down to key custody (StoreKey.swift's
	     `Variorum` vs `Variorum-dev` scopes). A group is part of an item's
	     identity and items never migrate between groups, so changing this
	     string later strands what was written under the old one. -->
	<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)$(PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER)</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
